# triclinic-reach.test with a Python simulation on the CPU
# (D[python-triclinic-npt], D241, #258): a narrow tilted cell that the
# barostat of a simulation shrinks until the pairlist distance is well
# beyond half of the least of a_x, b_y, c_z. At every frame the potential
# energy of the run is the sum over every image of every pair within the
# cutoff (Inputs/triclinic_reach.py). A Python simulation has the neighbor
# matrix (#270), so the stop of the groups below their reach (D242) is not
# one of a Python simulation.
#
# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/triclinic_reach.py %t python CPU MATRIX | FileCheck %s

# CHECK:      79 frames, 79 with the reach beyond half of the least of the diagonal
# CHECK-NEXT: half of the least of the diagonal well below the reach
# CHECK-NEXT: frames whose potential is not the sum over all images: 0
